# Validation And Release

- Canonical change-area → validation map, validation modes, and packaging/
  versioning policy: root `AGENTS.md` (Validation Modes, Validation By Change
  Area, Packaging And Versioning). Do not maintain a second full map here.
- Choose validation from that map by changed area. Domain skills may name their
  focused suite without copying the whole repository list.
- Validation modes: automatic subscription triage is non-executing inspection;
  authorized implementation/repair/finalization runs required affected checks;
  readiness assessment reports evidence/gaps and executes only when authorized.
- Normal development targets `beta`; `main` is for promotion and release workflows.
- Do not weaken CI to make checks pass.
- Keep the job name in `.github/workflows/copilot-setup-steps.yml` exactly `copilot-setup-steps`.
- Treat `SpectrumFederation/SpectrumFederation.toc` as the authoritative source for addon version, interface value, and load order whenever a task touches addon packaging or release/version logic. Packaged child TOC files must stay on the same Version and Interface values.
- Version bumps follow deterministic `release_required` classification for
  packaged addon/release-packaging changes. Instruction/docs/infra-only changes
  do not require a bump when the TOC format is already valid for the branch. A
  repair iteration does not automatically require another increment when the PR
  version is already valid for delivery.
- For UI layout, sizing, callbacks, events, timers, listeners, queues,
  inspection, sync, cache, or retry changes, prefer existing Lua 5.1 tests that
  assert bounded execution, convergence, and relevant behavioral sequences. See
  `SpectrumFederation/AGENTS.md` Client Stability.
